  "steps": [
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>Start</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Locate the RAM, SSD and GPU mounting points</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>CPU, cooler, PSU and cables are fitted. No power while assembling. No OS or cover needed.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Any order. Not every bench part is needed.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>RAM</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Read the labels and choose two RAM modules</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Identical DDR4, 8 GB each, 16 GB total.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Every value matches; fitting is not enough.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>RAM</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Fit RAM in A2 and B2: open the latch, align the notch, push in</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Press Trigger once on the latch, then hold RAM with Grip. Half-inserted is not connected.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> The latch closes itself when fully seated. The other end stays fixed.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>SSD</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Read the labels and choose one SSD</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>SATA 2.5-inch, ≥500 GB and ≥600 TBW.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Both values pass. TBW is not capacity.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>SSD</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Hold the case handle with Grip and move your hand around the base</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>The case follows your hand. Do not twist your wrist.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> The SSD tray mount behind the board is visible.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>SSD</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Push the SSD tray fully along the rails, then tighten its screw</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Tray: hold Grip. Screw: hold Trigger. The SSD is already on the tray; no underside screws.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> The tray is seated and does not move.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>SSD</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Push the SATA data and SATA power plugs fully in</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Hold each plug with Trigger. Seating the tray does not connect cables.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Both SSD cables are connected.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>GPU</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Read the labels and choose one GPU</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>VRAM ≥8 GB; card power ≤150 W.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Both values pass. Use card power, not PSU power.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>GPU</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Seat the GPU in the primary slot, screw it, plug in PCIe 8-pin</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Card: hold Grip. Screw and plug: hold Trigger. Primary slot: the long one wired to the CPU. The 6+2 plug is already joined.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Card fully seated, screw tight, plug fully in. Insertion alone does not secure it.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>Check my work</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Select Check my work on the task panel</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Wait 3 seconds.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> W2 passed means done.</color></size>"
    },
    {
      "text_en": "<size=24><color=#5B6B7F>If not passed</color></size>\n<size=46><b>Read the result, then correct and check again</b></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#4A5A6E>Incomplete: seating/fastener/cable. W2 failure: part/slot.</color></size>\n\n<size=34><color=#2E7D32><b>✓</b> Before removal, release latch/cable/screw. System fault: tell researcher.</color></size>"
    }
  ],
